[{"id":"marker0","name":"Swarentef Volcano","legend":"Dormant volcano. Height: 3721 m."},{"id":"marker1","name":"Dunsfordge Hot Springs","legend":"A geothermal springs with naturally heated water that provide relaxation and medicinal benefits. Average temperature is 20°C."},{"id":"marker2","name":"Axbrigh Healing Stream","legend":"This legendary water source is whispered about in ancient tales and believed to possess mystical properties. The spring emanates crystal-clear water, shimmering with an otherworldly iridescence that sparkles even in the dimmest light."},{"id":"marker3","name":"Stanton — silver mining town","legend":"Stanton is a mining town of 3215 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker4","name":"Sidgetonton — silver mining town","legend":"Sidgetonton is a mining town of 1135 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker5","name":"Pickerton — silver mining town","legend":"Pickerton is a mining town of 4450 people just nearby the silver mine."},{"id":"marker6","name":"Marlmondge Bridge","legend":"A lengthy bridge spans over the Skipton River near Marlmondge."},{"id":"marker7","name":"Padsle Bridge","legend":"An old crossing of the Padsle River, rarely used since the old waypoints crumbled."},{"id":"marker8","name":"The Frozen Shark","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious dressed garlic with green wine is served here."},{"id":"marker9","name":"The Honest Bear","legend":"A big and famous roadside tavern. Delicious pan-fried deer with brown liquor is served here."},{"id":"marker10","name":"Blandbury Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker11","name":"Stotham Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker12","name":"Caltonzanese Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker13","name":"Albronedian Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker14","name":"Finewich Lighthouse","legend":"A lighthouse to serve as a beacon for ships in the open sea."},{"id":"marker15","name":"Rockington Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Herthers Invasion. \r\nDate: July 12, 1677 Dunster Era."},{"id":"marker16","name":"Hatford Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Boverish War. \r\nDate: May 15, 1674 Dunster Era."},{"id":"marker17","name":"Merham Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Mazionian Campaign. \r\nDate: May 24, 1656 Dunster Era."},{"id":"marker18","name":"Cudbury Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Warbury Conquest. \r\nDate: September 11, 1419 Dunster Era."},{"id":"marker19","name":"Seaford Battlefield","legend":"A historical battle of the Gatham Conquest. \r\nDate: July 31, 1666 Dunster Era."},{"id":"marker20","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=6936455213449\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=6936455213449\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker21","name":"Dungeon","legend":"<div>Undiscovered dungeon. See <a href=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=6936455214830\" target=\"_blank\">One page dungeon</a></div><iframe style=\"pointer-events: none;\" src=\"https://watabou.github.io/one-page-dungeon/?seed=6936455214830\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker22","name":"Kirdenley Monster","legend":"Legends say a relic monster of 17 m long inhabits Kirdenley Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker23","name":"Haylesto Monster","legend":"Whispers say a relic monster of 12 m long inhabits Haylesto Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker24","name":"Masalton Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 20 m long."},{"id":"marker25","name":"Hertleho Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 24 m long."},{"id":"marker26","name":"Newbigton Ghoul","legend":"Journeying folk speak of a big Ghoul who inhabits Newbigton hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker27","name":"Cochamney Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Witnesses of Tiveridge."},{"id":"marker28","name":"Warescom Palm Grove","legend":"A palm grove sacred to local Stans Faith."},{"id":"marker29","name":"Brashorewes Rats","legend":"A gang of forest brigands."},{"id":"marker30","name":"Darwick Apes","legend":"A gang of forest brigands."},{"id":"marker31","name":"Buckington Bears","legend":"A gang of forest robbers."},{"id":"marker32","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker33","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker34","name":"Pirates","legend":"Pirate ships have been spotted in these waters."},{"id":"marker35","name":"Horsbuton Sculpture","legend":"An ancient sculpture. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">༼༮༰༩ༀ༐༗༢༗༹༈༡༒༵༮༃༜༷༖༹༧༡༒༾༐༭༮༓༧༼༧༴༂༫༊༇༷༈༹༭༣༣༤༚༯༃༆༭༼༪༐༲༅༦༬༑༙༓༒༿༫༽༊༸༇༚༄༨༌༲༠ༀ༛༯༽༿༕༵༉༲༅༾༩༹༬༪༓༹༼༶༩༕༒༱༱༂༦</div>"},{"id":"marker36","name":"Totlesey Idol","legend":"An ancient idol. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">᠐ᡑᠠᠰᡀᢋᢓᡁᡲᠳᡮᡝᡐᢒᡮᠿᡗᡆᠧᠧᡳᠳᡜᠳᡱᡙᢦᢞᠨᡱᢠᡎᡓᠱᢂᢋᡭᢁᠭᢏᡔᡞᡔ᠑ᢒᡗᡏᠵᡡᡆ᠀ᢥᡖᠼᢟᢂ</div>"},{"id":"marker37","name":"Norforden Pillar","legend":"An ancient pillar. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">\ud802𐠢\ud802 𐠡𐠄\udc17\ud802𐠡\udc24\ud802\ud802𐠨\udc19\udc03\ud802𐠜\ud802𐠛 \udc01\ud802𐠍𐠨𐠍\udc33𐠒\udc35\udc38\udc22\udc21\udc28\udc38𐠂\ud802\ud802\ud802𐠍\udc1a\udc35\udc2e\ud802\ud802\ud802𐠱\udc2e\udc13𐠮\udc1b𐠟\udc35\udc29\ud802\ud802𐠡\ud802𐠮\udc1c\ud802𐠷\ud802\ud802\ud802𐠊 \ud802𐠱\udc30</div>"},{"id":"marker38","name":"Brampton Megalith","legend":"An ancient megalith. It has an inscription, but no one can translate it:\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.8em; line-break: anywhere;\">᠀ᡴᢞᢡᢀᠭᢠᡲᡭᡙᡰᠰᡞᢓᢓᢜᢟᡠᢠᡕᡠᢠᡱᢤᡔᡱᢦᠪᡡᡱ᠒ᠨᢂ᠒ᡎᡏᢢᡟᢜᠳᠨᡡᡙᢒᠵᢥᡕᡞᠾᢀᢓᡐᡀᢥᡭᢞᢓᠨᡡᡍᢋᡐ᠑ᠪᠽ</div>"},{"id":"marker39","name":"Ruined Settlement","legend":"Ruins of an ancient settlement. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker40","name":"Ruined Pyramid","legend":"Ruins of an ancient pyramid. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker41","name":"Ruined City","legend":"Ruins of an ancient city. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker42","name":"Ruined Town","legend":"Ruins of an ancient town. Untold riches may lie within."},{"id":"marker43","name":"Witham Collection","legend":"A vast collection of knowledge, including many rare and ancient tomes."},{"id":"marker44","name":"Travelling Wonderous Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this wonderous circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker45","name":"Travelling Unmissable Circus","legend":"Roll up, roll up, this unmissable circus is here for a limited time only."},{"id":"marker46","name":"Salsearen Melee","legend":"Warriors from around the land gather for a melee of speed in Salsearen, with fame, fortune and favour on offer to the victor."},{"id":"marker47","name":"Bolboke Fair","legend":"A fair is being held in Bolboke, with all manner of local and foreign goods and services on offer."},{"id":"marker48","name":"Minor Jetty","legend":"A small location along the Felborne River to launch boats from sits here, along with a weary looking owner, willing to sell passage along the river."},{"id":"marker49","name":"Lions migration","legend":"A huge group of lions are migrating, whether part of their annual routine, or something more extraordinary."},{"id":"marker50","name":"Osterbot carnival","legend":"A carnival has been organised at Osterbot as a chance to gather the local elders of the area together to be merry, make alliances and scheme around the crisis."},{"id":"marker51","name":"Perculiar mirage","legend":"This perculiar mirage has been luring travellers out of their way for eons."},{"id":"marker52","name":"Olterton Hole","legend":"The Olterton Hole. Locals claim that it is endlessly deep and unexplored."},{"id":"marker53","name":"Malingle Tomb","legend":"A sprawling necropolis built within a labyrinthine network of catacombs. Its halls are lined with countless alcoves, each housing the remains of the departed, while the distant sound of rattling bones fills the air"},{"id":"marker54","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/1248\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker55","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/5107\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker56","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/2557\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker57","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/748\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker58","name":"Random encounter","legend":"<div>You have encountered a character.</div><iframe src=\"https://deorum.vercel.app/encounter/6020\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups\"></iframe>"},{"id":"marker59","name":"Random encou